TITLE:: SnapCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that snaps notes to the nearest grid line defined by a musical resolution.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/RightCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SnapCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: that snaps an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes (e.g. from LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#*selectedNotes::) to the nearest beat subdivision. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

It accepts a positive integer CODE::resolution:: between 1 and 16, representing the fraction of a beat (1/N beats):
LIST::
## CODE::1::: Whole beat (every 1.0 beat, matching the vertical beat lines)
## CODE::2::: Half beat (every 0.5 beats)
## CODE::4::: Quarter beat (every 0.25 beats)
## CODE::8::: Eighth beat (every 0.125 beats)
## CODE::16::: Sixteenth beat (every 0.0625 beats)
::

Each note's start time is shifted in the closest direction to the nearest multiple of CODE::1.0 / resolution:: beats while preserving duration. Timing edits on LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: reposition the note view automatically.

LINK::#-beforeImage:: records the start and stop time of each note whose start would change. A note already on the grid is left out, so an edit that changes nothing is not an undo step. LINK::#-restore:: writes those times back and repositions the view.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::SnapCommand::. Takes no arguments; snapping is implemented by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SnapCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: afterImage
The start and stop time of each note in the before-image, after LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary passed to LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: before
The LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: returned by LINK::#-beforeImage::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime::, or CODE::nil:: when CODE::before:: is empty.

METHOD:: beforeImage
The start and stop time of each selected note whose start would snap to a new grid line.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime::, or CODE::nil:: when every selected note is already on the grid.

METHOD:: execute
Snaps each note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: to the grid implied by CODE::\resolution::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::snapToGrid::) and CODE::\resolution:: (an LINK::Classes/Integer:: from 1 to 16).

METHOD:: restore
Writes CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime:: from an image back onto each note and repositions its view.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime::, or CODE::nil::.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(1.2, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	paintFunc: {},
	moveFunc: { |view, start, stop| ("Moved to " ++ start ++ ".." ++ stop).postln; }
);
note.stop(2.2);

var snapCmd = SnapCommand.new;

// Snap to nearest quarter note (resolution = 4)
snapCmd.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	resolution: 4
));
)
::

PRIVATE:: prEachNote, prGridSpacing
